{"id": 95, "ts": 1784169119.0558527, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I acknowledge your point, Agent\u202f2, that we have no direct evidence of Candidate\u202fC\u2019s operational reliability or stress\u2011resilience. However, we also lack any concrete example of Candidate\u202fB\u2019s decision quality under safety\u2011critical pressure \u2013 the very scenario where a pilot\u2019s judgment can prevent an incident. The only data we have for B are general statements about handling stress well and being conscientious, but no observed decision\u2011making record.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC demonstrably anticipates dangerous situations, perceives complex connections, and possesses excellent spatial vision \u2013 all indicators of superior situational awareness and rapid, accurate decision\u2011making in the cockpit. Moreover, C\u2019s very good leadership qualities suggest he can guide the crew effectively during long\u2011haul operations. While C\u2019s difficulty taking criticism and occasional disorganization are concerns, they are not yet proven to impair safety, whereas B\u2019s documented grumpiness, uncooperativeness, pretentious tone, and weak memory for numbers directly threaten crew cooperation and information accuracy.\nGiven the critical need for decisive, safety\u2011focused cognition on international routes, and the absence of evidence that B can consistently make high\u2011quality decisions under pressure, I maintain my provisional recommendation for **Candidate\u202fC** as the stronger overall fit."}
